6-10-30","vl":"French West Africa"},{"qid":"Q962","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flag of Benin.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q962","kind":"coat","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Coat of arms of Benin.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P94","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q962","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q16669148","value_label":"Patrice Talon","from_t":2016.2622950819673,"to_t":2026.3917808219178,"title":"President of the Republic of Benin","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Patrice Talon"},{"qid":"Q962","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q206719","value_label":"Mathieu Kérékou","from_t":1996.2568306010928,"to_t":2006.2575342465752,"title":"President of the Republic of Benin","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Mathieu Kérékou"},{"qid":"Q962","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q206719","value_label":"Mathieu Kérékou","from_t":1980.2568306010928,"to_t":1991.2547945205479,"title":"President of the Republic of Benin","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Mathieu Kérékou"},{"qid":"Q962","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q29196","value_label":"Thomas Boni Yayi","from_t":2006.2602739726028,"to_t":2016.2622950819673,"title":"President of the Republic of Benin","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Thomas Boni Yayi"},{"qid":"Q962","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q336218","value_label":"Nicéphore Soglo","from_t":1991.2547945205479,"to_t":1996.2568306010928,"title":"President of the Republic of Benin","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Nicéphore Soglo"},{"qid":"Q962","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q130442","value_label":"Flag of Benin.svg","from_t":1959.8739726027397,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Benin","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Benin"}],"people":{"Q24951128":{"label":"Romuald Wadagni","description":"President of Benin (born 1976)","enwiki":"Romuald Wadagni","summary":"Kossi Mbueke Romuald Wadagni (born 20 June 1976) is a Beninese politician and businessman who has served as the ninth president of Benin since 2026. Prior to that, he served as Minister of Economy and Finance under President Patrice Talon from 2016 to 2026, and worked for the consulting firm Deloitte prior to entering politics.","image":"Romuald Wadagni March 2026.jpg","birth":1976.467213114754,"death":null},"Q29035":{"label":"Pascal Koupaki","description":"Beninese politician","enwiki":"Pascal Koupaki","summary":"Pascal Irénée Koupaki (born 18 May 1951) is a Beninese politician who served as Prime Minister of Benin from May 2011 to August 2013. Koupaki worked as an official at the Central Bank of West African States (BCEAO) and the International Monetary Fund (IMF), and he was Director of the Cabinet of the Prime Minister from 1996 to 1998. Under President Yayi Boni, Koupaki was Minister of Finance from 2006 to 2007 and then Minister of State for the Exploration, Development, and Evaluation of Public Policy from 2007 to 2011.\nUnder President Patrice Talon, Koupaki has been Secretary-General of the Presidency since 2016.","image":"Pascal Koupaki 2012 (cropped).jpg","birth":1951.3287671232877,"death":null},"Q3241966":{"label":"Lionel Zinsou","description":"French investment banker, economist and private banker","enwiki":"Lionel Zinsou","summary":"Lionel Zinsou (born 23 October 1953) is a French–Beninese economist and investment banker who was Prime Minister of Benin from 2015 to 2016. Since June 2017, he has been the president of Terra Nova, a centre-left French think tank.","image":"Lionel Zinsou 2017.jpg","birth":1954.8082191780823,"death":null},"Q16669148":{"label":"Patrice Talon","description":"President of Benin between 2016 and 2026","enwiki":"Patrice Talon","summary":"Patrice Guillaume Athanase Talon (born 1 May 1958) is a Beninese politician and businessman who has been the first president of the Senate since 2026. He previously served as the eighth president of Benin from 2016 to 2026.","image":"Patrice Talon at USAID HQ (4) (cropped).jpg","birth":1958.3287671232877,"death":null},"Q206719":{"label":"Mathieu Kérékou","description":"politician (1933-2015)","enwiki":"Mathieu Kérékou","summary":"Mathieu Kérékou (French pronunciation: [ma.tjø ke.ʁe.ku]; 2 September 1933 – 14 October 2015) was a Beninese politician and revolutionary who served as president of the People's Republic of Benin from 1972 to 1991 and the Republic of Benin from 1996 to 2006.\nAfter seizing power in a military coup, he ruled the country for 18 years under an officially Marxist–Leninist ideology, before he was stripped of his powers by the National Conference of 1990. He was defeated in the 1991 presidential election but was returned to the presidency in the 1996 election and controversially re-elected in 2001.","image":"Mathieu Kérékou 2006Feb10.JPG","birth":1933.668493150685,"death":2015.7835616438356},"Q29196":{"label":"Thomas Boni Yayi","description":"Beninese politician and Former President of Benin","enwiki":"Thomas Boni Yayi","summary":"Thomas Boni Yayi (born 1 July 1951) is a Beninese banker and politician who was the president of Benin from 2006 to 2016. He took office after winning the March 2006 presidential election and was re-elected to a second term in March 2011. He also served as the chairperson of the African Union from 29 January 2012 to 27 January 2013 and currently serves as a senator since 30 July 2026.","image":"Yayi Boni.jpg","birth":1952.4972677595629,"death":null},"Q336218":{"label":"Nicéphore Soglo","description":"Prime Minister of Benin","enwiki":"Nicéphore Soglo","summary":"Nicéphore Dieudonné Soglo (born 29 November 1934) is a Beninese politician who was Prime Minister of Benin from 1990 to 1991 and President from 1991 to 1996. He was Mayor of Cotonou from 2003 to 2015. Soglo was married to Rosine Vieyra Soglo.","image":"Nicéphore Soglo - mars 2012.jpg","birth":1934.9095890410958,"death":null}},"media":{"Flag of Benin.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Flag_of_Benin.svg/330px-Flag_of_Benin.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Benin.svg","author":"Drawn by User:SKopp, rewritten by User:Gabbe","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Benin.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Coat_of_arms_of_Benin.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Benin.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Benin.svg","author":"Tinynanorobots, Fenn-O-maniC","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"Romuald Wadagni March 2026.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Romuald_Wadagni_March_2026.jpg/330px-Romuald_Wadagni_March_2026.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Romuald_Wadagni_March_2026.jpg","author":"Bibamad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},"Pascal Koupaki 2012 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/24/Pascal_Koupaki_2012_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pascal_Koupaki_2012_(cropped).jpg","author":"European Union","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"Lionel Zinsou 2017.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lionel_Zinsou_2017.jpg/330px-Lionel_Zinsou_2017.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lionel_Zinsou_2017.jpg","author":"Inter-American Dialogue","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"},"Patrice Talon at USAID HQ (4) (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Patrice_Talon_at_USAID_HQ_%284%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Patrice_Talon_at_USAID_HQ_%284%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source